{%- comment -%}
  OnRepeat buy bar — the permanent PDP purchase bar.

  One self-contained component: markup, styles and behaviour in this single
  snippet, inlined into every product render. Nothing here references an
  external versioned asset, so Shopify's page cache can never pair this
  markup with stale styling or script.

  Layout — a FLOATING CARD of two rows:

      (  [M] [L] [XL]              Size guide  )
      (  [img]  ₹1,394             ( ADD TO BAG ) )
      (  TRY ON  Only 1 left in L                )

  WHY THE SIZE RAIL IS HERE (2026-08-27 rebuild)
  Every product in this catalogue is single-option — Size, three to six
  values. That is small enough to put the whole variant set on the bar, and
  once it is there four separate problems in the old bar close at once:

  1. The old bar printed a bare "2 left". That was the stock of
     selected_or_first_available_variant, while product-variant-picker
     deliberately clears the pre-checked radio before paint — so the number
     described a size that was explicitly NOT selected, and was wrong for
     anyone wanting a different one. Stock is now only ever stated with the
     size it belongs to, and only once a size has actually been chosen.
  2. The old bar had two buttons (bag + BUY NOW) that opened the SAME size
     sheet and diverged only afterwards, while their accessible names
     promised outcomes neither delivered. There is now one action, and its
     label always names what the next tap does.
  3. The selected size was never shown at all, though it gated the purchase.
  4. Crimson was doing three jobs (CTA fill, bag outline, discount badge).
     It is now spent only on the primary action; the discount reverted to
     recessive text that actually passes contrast.

  SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH
  The rail does not hold its own state. A chip tap checks the matching radio
  inside <variant-selects> and dispatches a bubbling 'change', so the theme's
  own picker performs the variant switch exactly as if the shopper had used
  the on-page control. We then re-render from the resulting 'variant:change'.
  Two pickers that each held their own idea of the selection is precisely the
  class of bug that produced the phantom "2 left".

  ADD TO CART
  The CTA drives the theme's own hidden .product-form__submit rather than
  posting to /cart/add itself, so AJAX cart, cart-drawer opening, error
  handling and sold-out relabelling all remain the theme's tested code path.

  Behaviour contract (unchanged from the previous bar):
  - Floats clear of the screen: 8px in from each side, 12px + iOS safe area
    above the bottom, no rounded-display clipping, no home-indicator overlap.
  - Solid near-opaque background ON PURPOSE: backdrop-filter blur painted a
    white halo outside the card on phones (bisected live, 2026-08-06,
    reproduced in Chromium and iOS Safari). Do not reintroduce it here.
  - Price is the automatic-discount NET (flat tier subtracted first, then the
    percentage on the remainder — mirroring how Shopify applies them).
  - INR prints whole rupees; US visitors keep theme.money's converted display.
  - Publishes its height as --onrepeat-sticky-reserve and reserves footer runway.
  - Virtual Try-On sits outside the availability gate: half the catalogue is
    sold out at any time and try-on must stay reachable there.

  Params: product, product_form_id, section_id
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign bb_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant

  assign bb_size_index = -1
  for bb_opt in product.options_with_values
    assign bb_opt_handle = bb_opt.name | downcase
    if bb_opt_handle contains 'size'
      assign bb_size_index = forloop.index0
      break
    endif
  endfor
  assign bb_has_size_rail = false
  if bb_size_index >= 0 and product.options_with_values.size == 1 and product.has_only_default_variant == false
    assign bb_has_size_rail = true
  endif
  if bb_size_index < 0
    assign bb_size_index = 0
  endif

  comment
    Reward settings — the same source the ladder, offer line and cart rail
    read, so every surface states the same numbers.
  endcomment
  assign bb_min = settings.reward_tier1_amount | default: 1499 | times: 100
  assign bb_pct = settings.reward_percent | default: 5
  assign bb_t2 = settings.reward_tier2_amount | default: 3000 | times: 100
  assign bb_a2 = settings.reward_tier2_flat | default: 300 | times: 100
  assign bb_t3 = settings.reward_tier3_amount | default: 5000 | times: 100
  assign bb_a3 = settings.reward_tier3_flat | default: 700 | times: 100

  assign bb_flat = 0
  if bb_t3 > 0 and bb_variant.price >= bb_t3
    assign bb_flat = bb_a3
  elsif bb_t2 > 0 and bb_variant.price >= bb_t2
    assign bb_flat = bb_a2
  endif
  assign bb_keep = 100 | minus: bb_pct
  assign bb_net = bb_variant.price | minus: bb_flat | times: bb_keep | divided_by: 100

  comment
    Same >0 guards as the JS render() — a reward setting of 0 must not print
    '0% off applied' server-side only for the first variant change to snap it
    away.
  endcomment
  assign bb_on_offer = false
  if bb_min > 0 and bb_pct > 0 and bb_variant.price >= bb_min
    assign bb_on_offer = true
  endif

  capture bb_badge
    if bb_on_offer
      echo bb_pct
      echo '%'
      if bb_flat > 0
        echo ' + '
        render 'money-display', amount: bb_flat, style: 'no_zeros'
      endif
      echo ' off applied'
    elsif bb_variant.compare_at_price > bb_variant.price
      assign bb_sale_pct = bb_variant.compare_at_price | minus: bb_variant.price | times: 100.0 | divided_by: bb_variant.compare_at_price | round
      echo bb_sale_pct
      echo '% off'
    endif
  endcapture

  comment
    Scarcity dot threshold. Most polos sit at 1-4 units, so dotting every
    chip at <=3 would light the whole rail and stop meaning anything. Default
    is 1 — the merchant can widen it without touching code.
  endcomment
  assign bb_dot_at = settings.buy_bar_dot_at | default: 1

  capture bb_sc_key
    render 'size-chart-key', product: product
  endcapture
  assign bb_sc_key = bb_sc_key | strip

  comment
    The size sheet's trigger contract, captured once. Both the "Size guide"
    link and the optional Buy Now button are sheet triggers, so they read the
    same values rather than each building their own.
  endcomment
  assign bb_thumb_url = bb_variant.featured_media | default: product.featured_media | image_url: width: 120

  comment
    The size-chart drawer the bar opens. The page normally comes from the
    variant picker's block setting, but that block is disabled on these
    templates, and a disabled block is absent from section.blocks — its
    setting cannot be read at all. So the page is resolved from a theme
    setting, falling back to the 'size-chart' page every product template
    already points at.

    Its own id, not the picker's: if the picker is ever switched back on both
    drawers exist, and reusing one id would put two elements with the same id
    in the document and break whichever opener resolved second.
  endcomment
  assign bb_chart_page = settings.size_chart_page
  if bb_chart_page == blank
    assign bb_chart_page = pages['size-chart']
  endif
  assign bb_chart_modal_id = 'OnRepeatBuyBarSizeChart-' | append: section_id | append: '-' | append: product.id
  assign bb_chart_title = bb_chart_page.title | default: 'Size chart'
-%}
{%- capture bb_sheet_variants -%}[{%- for v in product.variants -%}{"id":{{ v.id }},"title":{{ v.title | json }},"available":{{ v.available }}}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}{%- endfor -%}]{%- endcapture -%}
{%- capture bb_sheet_price -%}{%- render 'onrepeat-sheet-price', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}

<style>
  onrepeat-buy-bar {
    position: fixed;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    z-index: 20;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    /* The product page scrolls horizontally inside the gallery slider, which
       widens the box a fixed left:0/right:0 element resolves against — below
       ~375px the card was running past the right edge. Clamping pins it back. */
    max-width: 100vw;
    /* WebKit's documented pattern: max() keeps the card clear of rounded
       corners, landscape notches and the home indicator in every toolbar
       state, and still gives a constant margin when the insets are 0. */
    padding: 0
      max(8px, env(safe-area-inset-left, 0px))
      max(12px, calc(12px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px)))
      max(8px, env(safe-area-inset-right, 0px));
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__card {
    pointer-events: auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    max-width: 100%;
    padding: 10px;
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 0.5px solid rgba(26, 21, 18, 0.1);
    border-radius: 18px;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 28px rgba(26, 21, 18, 0.16), 0 2px 6px rgba(26, 21, 18, 0.06);
  }

  /* ── size rail ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .onrepeat-bb__sizes {
    display: flex;
    align-items: stretch;
    gap: 6px;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__chip {
    flex: 1 1 0;
    min-width: 38px;
    height: 40px;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    position: relative;
    padding: 0;
    border: 1px solid rgba(26, 21, 18, 0.16);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: #fff;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #1a1512;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background-color 0.14s ease, border-color 0.14s ease, color 0.14s ease;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__chip[aria-pressed='true'] {
    /* Ink, not crimson: the brand colour is reserved for the one action. */
    background: #1a1512;
    border-color: #1a1512;
    color: #fff;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__chip[disabled] {
    color: rgba(26, 21, 18, 0.3);
    border-color: rgba(26, 21, 18, 0.08);
    cursor: not-allowed;
    background: linear-gradient(
      to top left,
      transparent calc(50% - 0.6px),
      rgba(26, 21, 18, 0.22) 50%,
      transparent calc(50% + 0.6px)
    );
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__dot {
    position: absolute;
    top: 6px;
    right: 6px;
    width: 4px;
    height: 4px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #9a5200;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__chip[aria-pressed='true'] .onrepeat-bb__dot {
    background: #e9a23b;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__guide {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    height: 40px;
    padding: 0 10px;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    border: 0;
    background: none;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #6f625c;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  /* Asking for a size the shopper can already see needs a nudge, not a modal. */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .onrepeat-bb__sizes.is-asking .onrepeat-bb__chip:not([disabled]) {
      animation: onrepeat-bb-ask 0.42s ease;
    }
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__sizes.is-asking .onrepeat-bb__chip:not([disabled]) {
    border-color: #5c1011;
  }
  @keyframes onrepeat-bb-ask {
    0%, 100% { transform: translateY(0); }
    30% { transform: translateY(-3px); }
    60% { transform: translateY(0); }
  }

  /* ── main row ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .onrepeat-bb__main {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__thumb {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 48px;
    height: 48px;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0.5px solid rgba(26, 21, 18, 0.12);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: #efedea;
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  {%- comment -%}
    No overflow clip here. With try-on on, this element IS the minimised
    try-on tile, and its "ready" dot deliberately sits outside the 48px box at
    top/right -3px. This snippet's <style> is inline in the body and therefore
    wins over assets/vto.css on equal specificity, so `overflow: hidden` here
    silently ate the one signal that says a look is waiting. The image and the
    label carry their own radii instead — nothing needs the parent to cut it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  .onrepeat-bb__thumb img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
    border-radius: 10px;
  }
  /* With try-on switched off the tile is identity only: it must not advertise
     itself as pressable, and with no ring or dot to escape the box it keeps
     the clip. */
  .onrepeat-bb__thumb--static {
    cursor: default;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__thumb span {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    height: 15px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background: rgba(26, 21, 18, 0.86);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 7.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__price {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    min-width: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3px;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__net {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: #1a1512;
    white-space: nowrap;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__sub {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 2px 6px;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 1.25;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__sub[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
  /* #6f625c is 5.87:1 on white. The old #a4968f at 10.24px was 2.86:1 — the
     strike is the half of the price line that does the persuading, and it
     was the least readable thing on the card. */
  .onrepeat-bb__was {
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #6f625c;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__off {
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #6f625c;
  }
  /* #9a5200 is 5.86:1; the old #d97706 was 3.19:1. */
  .onrepeat-bb__stock {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 5px;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #9a5200;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__stock[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__stock::before {
    content: '';
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 5px;
    height: 5px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #9a5200;
  }
  /* An error the shopper has to be told about — "the maximum quantity of this
     item is already in your cart" and friends. The form carries
     data-hide-errors, so without this the request fails and the bar says
     nothing at all. */
  .onrepeat-bb__err {
    /* Shopify's cart messages run long ("All 2 CANE Knit Polo — Slate are in
       your cart."). Unclamped it wrapped to three lines and grew the card by
       ~40px mid-interaction, which is worse than the silence it replaced.
       Two lines, then ellipsis; the colour does the flagging, so there is no
       bullet to strand halfway down a wrapped line. */
    display: -webkit-box;
    -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
    -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
    overflow: hidden;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: #b3401a;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__err[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__cta {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    /* Sized to the widest label the button ever carries ("Select size", 140px
       at this size and weight) so it holds still through every state change.
       At 132px it shrank 8px the instant it was tapped, moving the card under
       the thumb that was still on it. */
    min-width: 140px;
    height: 52px;
    padding: 0 20px;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: rgb(var(--color-base-button, 92 16 17));
    color: rgb(var(--color-base-button-text, 255 255 255));
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    cursor: pointer;
    /* The icon and the word sit on one line and the min-width above is wider
       than every label, so the card never resizes under a thumb that is still
       on the glass. */
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: transform 0.1s ease, opacity 0.18s ease;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__cta[data-state='idle'] {
    background: #fff;
    color: #1a1512;
    border: 1.5px solid rgba(26, 21, 18, 0.22);
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__cta[data-state='gone'] {
    background: #efedea;
    color: #8a817b;
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }
  /* ── in flight ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     The theme sets aria-busy on its own submit button and animates a dot
     loader inside it — but that button is display:none on this template, so
     the loader ran where nobody could see it and the whole response to a tap
     was the 28% opacity drop this replaces. Two sequential requests take
     around 1.7s, which is a long time to look like nothing happened.
     -------------------------------------------------------------------- */
  .onrepeat-bb__cta[data-state='busy'] {
    background: #6e2122;
    cursor: progress;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__cta[data-state='done'] {
    background: #2f6b4f;
    cursor: default;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__spin {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 15px;
    height: 15px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 2px solid rgb(var(--color-base-button-text, 255 255 255) / 0.35);
    border-top-color: rgb(var(--color-base-button-text, 255 255 255));
    animation: onrepeat-bb-spin 0.6s linear infinite;
  }
  @keyframes onrepeat-bb-spin {
    to { transform: rotate(360deg); }
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__tick {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 15px;
    height: 15px;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__tick path {
    fill: none;
    stroke: #fff;
    stroke-width: 2.6;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
    stroke-dasharray: 22;
    stroke-dashoffset: 22;
    animation: onrepeat-bb-draw 0.28s ease forwards;
  }
  @keyframes onrepeat-bb-draw {
    to { stroke-dashoffset: 0; }
  }
  /* A second signal, in case the button is under the thumb that just tapped it. */
  .onrepeat-bb__prog {
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline: 10px;
    inset-block-start: 0;
    height: 2px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: rgb(var(--color-base-button, 92 16 17) / 0.1);
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.15s ease;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__card { position: relative; }
  .onrepeat-bb__card[data-adding] .onrepeat-bb__prog { opacity: 1; }
  .onrepeat-bb__prog i {
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    width: 36%;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: rgb(var(--color-base-button, 92 16 17));
    animation: onrepeat-bb-slide 1s ease-in-out infinite;
  }
  @keyframes onrepeat-bb-slide {
    0% { transform: translateX(-100%); }
    100% { transform: translateX(320%); }
  }
  /* While the add is in flight the size cannot change under it. */
  .onrepeat-bb__card[data-adding] .onrepeat-bb__chip {
    pointer-events: none;
    opacity: 0.55;
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__cta:active {
    transform: scale(0.97);
  }
  .onrepeat-bb__chip:focus-visible,
  .onrepeat-bb__cta:focus-visible,
  .onrepeat-bb__guide:focus-visible,
  .onrepeat-bb__thumb:focus-visible,
  .onrepeat-bb__second:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid rgb(var(--color-base-button, 92 16 17));
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  /* Optional second action, off by default — see the snippet header. */
  .onrepeat-bb__second {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 8px;
    width: 100%;
    height: 40px;
    border: 1.5px solid rgba(26, 21, 18, 0.22);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: #fff;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #1a1512;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 359px) {
    .onrepeat-bb__card { padding: 8px; gap: 8px; }
    .onrepeat-bb__sizes { gap: 5px; }
    .onrepeat-bb__chip { min-width: 30px; font-size: 12.5px; }
    /* The guide used to be hidden at this width. It can't be now: the variant
       picker carried the page's other size-guide link and the picker is gone,
       so this is the only way in. Narrowed instead of dropped — six chips plus
       the link still fit 320px. */
    .onrepeat-bb__guide { padding: 0 6px; font-size: 11.5px; }
    .onrepeat-bb__cta { min-width: 122px; padding: 0 10px; font-size: 12px; }
    .onrepeat-bb__net { font-size: 18px; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .onrepeat-bb__cta, .onrepeat-bb__chip { transition: none; }
    .onrepeat-bb__cta:active { transform: none; }
    /* The spinner still has to read as "working", so it steps rather than
       sweeps instead of disappearing entirely. */
    .onrepeat-bb__spin { animation-duration: 1.2s; animation-timing-function: steps(8, end); }
    .onrepeat-bb__tick path { animation: none; stroke-dashoffset: 0; }
    .onrepeat-bb__prog i { animation: none; width: 100%; opacity: 0.5; }
  }
  @media screen and (min-width: 768px) {
    onrepeat-buy-bar {
      left: auto;
      right: var(--sp-5, 20px);
      bottom: var(--sp-5, 20px);
      justify-content: flex-end;
      padding: 0;
    }
    .onrepeat-bb__card {
      /* desktop docks bottom-right and sizes to content */
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 14px;
      padding: 10px 12px;
    }
    /* The row reads thumb, price, sizes, action — but the CTA lives inside
       .onrepeat-bb__main and `order` cannot move a child between flex
       containers. display:contents dissolves the wrapper so all four become
       direct children of the card and one order sequence governs them. */
    .onrepeat-bb__main { display: contents; }
    .onrepeat-bb__thumb { order: 1; }
    .onrepeat-bb__price { order: 2; flex: 0 1 auto; }
    .onrepeat-bb__sizes { order: 3; flex: 0 0 auto; }
    .onrepeat-bb__chip { flex: 0 0 auto; width: 44px; }
    .onrepeat-bb__cta { order: 4; }
    .onrepeat-bb__second { order: 5; width: auto; padding: 0 16px; }
  }
  @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {
    /* The bar covers the end of the page — reserve exactly its height
       (published as --onrepeat-sticky-reserve by the element) plus the float
       gap, so the footer scrolls fully clear. */
    body:has(onrepeat-buy-bar) .footer-copyright {
      padding-block-end: calc(
        var(--sp-5, 20px) + var(--onrepeat-sticky-reserve, 5rem) + 12px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px)
      );
    }
  }
</style>

{%- capture bb_variants_json -%}
  [{%- for v in product.variants -%}
    {
      "id":{{ v.id }},
      "title":{{ v.title | json }},
      "available":{{ v.available }},
      "option_value":{{ v.options[bb_size_index] | json }},
      "price":{{ v.price }},
      "compare_at_price":{% if v.compare_at_price %}{{ v.compare_at_price }}{% else %}null{% endif %},
      "inventory_quantity":{% if v.inventory_management == 'shopify' and v.inventory_policy != 'continue' %}{{ v.inventory_quantity }}{% else %}null{% endif %}
    }{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
  {%- endfor -%}]
{%- endcapture -%}

<onrepeat-buy-bar
  id="OnRepeatBuyBar-{{ section_id }}-{{ product.id }}"
  data-section-id="{{ section_id }}"
  data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
  data-picker="VariantPicker-{{ section_id }}-{{ product.id }}"
  data-promo-min="{{ bb_min }}"
  data-promo-pct="{{ bb_pct }}"
  data-flat-t2="{{ bb_t2 }}" data-flat-a2="{{ bb_a2 }}"
  data-flat-t3="{{ bb_t3 }}" data-flat-a3="{{ bb_a3 }}"
  data-dot-at="{{ bb_dot_at }}"
>
  {%- comment -%}
    The bar carries its own cart form.

    There is no product <form> on this page: purchasing was moved to the
    sticky bar plus the size sheet, and main-product's form was dropped with
    it — every [form="ProductForm-…"] reference on the page, the variant
    picker's radios included, points at an element that does not exist. So
    driving "the theme's hidden add-to-cart button" is not available here;
    there isn't one.

    This is the same three-element shape the size sheet uses and that the
    theme's ProductForm class is built around: action=/cart/add, is=product-form,
    a [name=id] input and a [type=submit][name=add]. Rendering our own keeps
    AJAX cart, cart-drawer opening and error handling on the theme's tested
    path without depending on page structure that is not there, and without
    reaching into the sheet's form and fighting whatever it has staged.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <form
    method="post"
    action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}"
    is="product-form"
    id="OnRepeatBuyBarForm-{{ section_id }}-{{ product.id }}"
    data-hide-errors="true"
    hidden
  >
    <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ bb_variant.id }}" data-bb-vid>
    <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">
    <button type="submit" name="add" class="product-form__submit" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"></button>
  </form>

  <div class="onrepeat-bb__card" role="region" aria-label="Buy {{ product.title | escape }}">
    <span class="onrepeat-bb__prog" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
    {%- comment -%}
      The button's own label changes are not announced, so the state is
      mirrored here for screen readers.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <span class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-bb-status></span>

    {%- comment -%}
      The rail. Rendered only for single-option size products (every product
      in this catalogue today); anything else falls back to the CTA opening
      the size sheet, exactly as before.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if bb_has_size_rail and product.available -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Literal strings, not | t with a | default fallback: a missing key
        returns the truthy string "Translation missing: …", so the default
        filter never fires and the shopper reads the error. These keys do not
        exist in the theme's locales.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="onrepeat-bb__sizes" role="group" aria-label="Choose a size" data-bb-sizes>
        {%- for v in product.variants -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign v_qty = nil
            if v.inventory_management == 'shopify' and v.inventory_policy != 'continue'
              assign v_qty = v.inventory_quantity
            endif
            assign v_dot = false
            if v.available and v_qty != nil and v_qty > 0 and v_qty <= bb_dot_at
              assign v_dot = true
            endif
          -%}
          <button
            type="button"
            class="onrepeat-bb__chip"
            data-bb-chip
            data-vid="{{ v.id }}"
            data-size="{{ v.options[bb_size_index] | escape }}"
            aria-pressed="false"
            {% unless v.available %}disabled aria-label="{{ v.options[bb_size_index] | escape }} — {{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t }}"{% endunless %}
          >{{ v.options[bb_size_index] | escape }}{% if v_dot %}<i class="onrepeat-bb__dot" aria-hidden="true"></i>{% endif %}</button>
        {%- endfor -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Opens the theme's own size-chart drawer — the same one the variant
          picker's "Size chart · Find my size" link opens, rendered from the
          shared snippet just below.

          The link always pointed here by aria-controls; what broke it was that
          the drawer was written inline inside the picker, so hiding the picker
          took the drawer off the page and the id resolved to nothing. The
          drawer is now rendered by the bar itself, so the link works whether
          the picker is on the page or not.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if bb_chart_page != blank -%}
          <button
            type="button"
            class="onrepeat-bb__guide"
            aria-controls="{{ bb_chart_modal_id }}"
            aria-expanded="false"
          >Size guide</button>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="onrepeat-bb__main">
      {%- comment -%}
        Try-on as a 48px tile rather than the full-width row it used to be.
        That row plus the old card ran 129px; this whole card measures 124px,
        so the rail is paid for and five pixels come back. It stays outside
        the availability gate — half the catalogue is sold out at any time and
        browsing is most of the traffic.

        settings.vto_enabled is the switch added when try-on was withdrawn
        from the live theme. With try-on off the tile is still worth its
        space: past the gallery the bar is otherwise a floating price with no
        referent, and the shopper is by then looking at a carousel of other
        garments. So it degrades to a plain thumbnail rather than vanishing.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if settings.vto_enabled -%}
        {%- render 'vto-button', product: product, placement: 'tile' -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- assign bb_tile_media = bb_variant.featured_media | default: product.featured_media -%}
        {%- if bb_tile_media != blank -%}
          <span class="onrepeat-bb__thumb onrepeat-bb__thumb--static" aria-hidden="true">
            {{- bb_tile_media.preview_image | image_url: width: 144 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '48,96,144', alt: '' -}}
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="onrepeat-bb__price">
        <b class="onrepeat-bb__net" data-bb-net>
          {%- if bb_on_offer -%}
            {%- render 'money-display', amount: bb_net, style: 'whole' -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- render 'money-display', amount: bb_variant.price, style: 'whole' -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        </b>
        {%- comment -%}
          No stock line on the server render: nothing is selected yet, and a
          stock figure without a size beside it is the bug this rebuild exists
          to remove.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="onrepeat-bb__sub" data-bb-sub {% unless bb_on_offer or bb_badge != blank %}hidden{% endunless %}>
          <s class="onrepeat-bb__was" data-bb-was>
            {%- if bb_on_offer -%}
              {%- render 'money-display', amount: bb_variant.price, style: 'whole' -%}
            {%- elsif bb_variant.compare_at_price > bb_variant.price -%}
              {%- render 'money-display', amount: bb_variant.compare_at_price, style: 'whole' -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          </s>
          <span class="onrepeat-bb__off" data-bb-off>{{ bb_badge }}</span>
          <span class="onrepeat-bb__stock" data-bb-stock hidden></span>
          <span class="onrepeat-bb__err" data-bb-err hidden></span>
        </span>
      </div>

      {%- if product.available -%}
        <button
          type="button"
          class="onrepeat-bb__cta"
          data-bb-cta
          data-add="Add to bag"
          data-adding="Adding"
          data-added="Added"
          data-sold-out="{{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t | escape }}"
          data-state="{% if bb_has_size_rail %}idle{% else %}ready{% endif %}"
        >{% if bb_has_size_rail %}Select size{% else %}Add to bag{% endif %}</button>
      {%- else -%}
        <button type="button" class="onrepeat-bb__cta" data-state="gone" disabled>{{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t }}</button>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Buy Now, off by default. Paired Add-to-bag / Buy-now is the Indian
      marketplace signature and reads as marketplace rather than brand, which
      is why the rebuild drops it — but the merchant can restore it from theme
      settings without code. When on, it routes through the existing size
      sheet in buynow mode, the path that is already Razorpay-safe.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if settings.buy_bar_show_buy_now and product.available -%}
      <button
        type="button"
        class="onrepeat-bb__second"
        data-sleek-open
        data-bb-gate
        data-mode="buynow"
        data-product-title="{{ product.title | escape }}"
        data-product-price="{{ bb_sheet_price | strip_newlines | escape }}"
        data-product-handle="{{ product.handle }}"
        data-sc-chart="{{ bb_sc_key | escape }}"
        data-product-image="{{ bb_thumb_url }}"
        data-variants='{{ bb_sheet_variants | strip_newlines | escape }}'
        data-selected=""
      >Buy now</button>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <script type="application/json" data-bb-variants>{{ bb_variants_json | strip_newlines | replace: '</', '<\/' }}</script>
</onrepeat-buy-bar>

{%- comment -%}
  Rendered OUTSIDE <onrepeat-buy-bar> deliberately. The host is
  pointer-events:none so taps fall through its padding, and a drawer nested
  inside it would inherit that and refuse every click.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- render 'size-chart-modal',
    modal_id: bb_chart_modal_id,
    product: product,
    chart_page: bb_chart_page,
    title: bb_chart_title -%}

<script>
  (function () {
    'use strict';
    if (customElements.get('onrepeat-buy-bar')) return;

    class OnRepeatBuyBar extends HTMLElement {
      connectedCallback() {
        this.netEl = this.querySelector('[data-bb-net]');
        this.subEl = this.querySelector('[data-bb-sub]');
        this.wasEl = this.querySelector('[data-bb-was]');
        this.offEl = this.querySelector('[data-bb-off]');
        this.stockEl = this.querySelector('[data-bb-stock]');
        this.ctaEl = this.querySelector('[data-bb-cta]');
        this.sizesEl = this.querySelector('[data-bb-sizes]');
        this.chips = Array.prototype.slice.call(this.querySelectorAll('[data-bb-chip]'));
        this.card = this.querySelector('.onrepeat-bb__card');
        this.selected = null;

        var json = this.querySelector('script[data-bb-variants]');
        try {
          this.variants = json ? JSON.parse(json.textContent) : [];
        } catch (e) {
          this.variants = [];
        }

        var n = (name) => parseInt(this.dataset[name], 10) || 0;
        this.cfg = {
          min: n('promoMin'), pct: n('promoPct'),
          t2: n('flatT2'), a2: n('flatA2'), t3: n('flatT3'), a3: n('flatA3'),
        };

        this.cartForm = document.getElementById(
          'OnRepeatBuyBarForm-' + this.dataset.sectionId + '-' + this.dataset.productId
        );
        this.vidInput = this.cartForm ? this.cartForm.querySelector('[data-bb-vid]') : null;

        this._onChip = (e) => {
          var chip = e.target.closest('[data-bb-chip]');
          if (!chip || chip.disabled) return;
          this.choose(chip.dataset.size);
        };
        if (this.sizesEl) this.sizesEl.addEventListener('click', this._onChip);

        // The on-page picker is the other way in. Listen to the radios
        // directly rather than to the theme's 'variant:change': that event is
        // emitted by the variant-selects re-render, which on this template
        // has no product form to re-render against. A plain change event is
        // what actually fires, and it fires synchronously.
        this._picker = this.picker;
        this._onPickerChange = (e) => {
          var r = e.target;
          if (!r || r.type !== 'radio' || !r.checked) return;
          var v = this.byOption(r.value);
          if (v) this.render(v, true);
        };
        if (this._picker) this._picker.addEventListener('change', this._onPickerChange);

        this._onCta = (e) => {
          var state = this.ctaEl.getAttribute('data-state');
          if (state === 'gone') return;
          if (state === 'idle') {
            e.preventDefault();
            this.ask();
            return;
          }
          this.submit();
        };
        if (this.ctaEl) this.ctaEl.addEventListener('click', this._onCta);

        // Kept as a belt-and-braces path: if a template ever does render a
        // real product form, the theme's event still keeps the rail honest.
        this._onVariantChange = (e) => {
          if (e && e.detail && e.detail.variant) this.render(e.detail.variant, true);
        };
        document.addEventListener('variant:change', this._onVariantChange);

        this.publishReserve();
        if ('ResizeObserver' in window && this.card) {
          this._ro = new ResizeObserver(() => this.publishReserve());
          this._ro.observe(this.card);
        } else {
          this._onWin = () => this.publishReserve();
          window.addEventListener('load', this._onWin);
          window.addEventListener('resize', this._onWin);
        }
      }

      disconnectedCallback() {
        document.removeEventListener('variant:change', this._onVariantChange);
        if (this._picker) this._picker.removeEventListener('change', this._onPickerChange);
        if (this.sizesEl) this.sizesEl.removeEventListener('click', this._onChip);
        if (this.ctaEl) this.ctaEl.removeEventListener('click', this._onCta);
        if (this._ro) this._ro.disconnect();
        if (this._onWin) {
          window.removeEventListener('load', this._onWin);
          window.removeEventListener('resize', this._onWin);
        }
      }

      get picker() {
        return document.getElementById(this.dataset.picker) || document.querySelector('variant-selects');
      }

      byOption(size) {
        return this.variants.filter((v) => v.option_value === size)[0] || null;
      }

      // Render immediately, then mirror the choice into the on-page picker so
      // the two controls always show the same size. The rail does not wait on
      // the picker to report back — on this template nothing would come.
      choose(size) {
        var v = this.byOption(size);
        if (!v || v.available === false) return;
        this.render(v, true);
        this.echoToPicker(size);
      }

      echoToPicker(size) {
        var picker = this._picker || this.picker;
        if (!picker) return;
        var radio = Array.prototype.slice
          .call(picker.querySelectorAll('input[type="radio"]'))
          .filter((r) => r.value === size)[0];
        if (!radio || radio.checked) return;
        radio.checked = true;
        // Bubbling change so the theme's own picker UI (and anything else
        // listening, such as the size gate) updates exactly as if the shopper
        // had tapped it there.
        radio.dispatchEvent(new Event('change', { bubbles: true }));
      }

      // The size is on screen a few pixels away; a modal would be a worse
      // answer than pointing at it.
      ask() {
        if (!this.sizesEl) return;
        this.sizesEl.classList.remove('is-asking');
        void this.sizesEl.offsetWidth;
        this.sizesEl.classList.add('is-asking');
        var first = this.chips.filter((c) => !c.disabled)[0];
        if (first) first.focus();
        window.setTimeout(() => this.sizesEl.classList.remove('is-asking'), 700);
      }

      // ── the CTA's visible state ──────────────────────────────────────
      // 'ready' | 'busy' | 'done' | 'error' | 'gone'. The label always names
      // what is happening, and the icon carries it for anyone who does not
      // read the label.
      setCta(state, label, icon) {
        if (!this.ctaEl) return;
        this.ctaEl.setAttribute('data-state', state);
        var mark = '';
        if (icon === 'spin') {
          mark = '<span class="onrepeat-bb__spin" aria-hidden="true"></span>';
        } else if (icon === 'tick') {
          mark = '<svg class="onrepeat-bb__tick" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 12.5l5.2 5.2L20 7"/></svg>';
        }
        this.ctaEl.innerHTML = mark + '<span>' + label + '</span>';
      }

      say(msg) {
        var el = this.querySelector('[data-bb-status]');
        if (el) el.textContent = msg;
      }

      showError(msg) {
        var el = this.querySelector('[data-bb-err]');
        if (!el) return;
        if (msg) {
          el.textContent = msg;
          el.hidden = false;
          // The scarcity line and a failure are two claims about the same
          // size; showing both at once reads as noise and stacks the card.
          if (this.stockEl) this.stockEl.hidden = true;
        } else {
          el.textContent = '';
          el.hidden = true;
          // Put the scarcity line back exactly as the last render left it —
          // otherwise "Only 1 left in L" disappears for good after one add.
          if (this.stockEl) this.stockEl.hidden = !this._stockVisible;
        }
      }

      // Stamp the chosen variant onto our own cart form and submit it, so
      // AJAX cart, the cart drawer and error handling all stay on the theme's
      // ProductForm path.
      submit() {
        if (this.adding) return;                      // no double-submits
        if (!this.cartForm || !this.vidInput || !this.selected) return;
        var v = this.byOption(this.selected);
        if (!v || v.available === false) return;
        var btn = this.cartForm.querySelector('[type="submit"][name="add"]');
        if (!btn) return;

        this.vidInput.value = v.id;
        this.adding = true;
        this.showError('');
        this.card.setAttribute('data-adding', '');
        this.ctaEl.setAttribute('aria-busy', 'true');
        this.setCta('busy', this.ctaEl.dataset.adding || 'Adding', 'spin');
        this.say('Adding ' + this.selected + ' to your bag');

        // The theme dispatches these once the add settles. Bound only for the
        // life of this submit so another surface's add can never drive our
        // button.
        var settle = (ok, msg) => {
          if (!this.adding) return;
          this.adding = false;
          window.clearTimeout(this._addTimer);
          document.removeEventListener('ajaxProduct:added', onAdded);
          document.removeEventListener('ajaxProduct:error', onError);
          this.ctaEl.removeAttribute('aria-busy');
          this.card.removeAttribute('data-adding');

          if (!ok) {
            this.setCta('ready', this.ctaEl.dataset.add || 'Add to bag', '');
            this.showError(msg || 'Could not add that. Please try again.');
            this.say(msg || 'Could not add that item');
            return;
          }

          // Held, not flashed: the drawer is opening over this, and a
          // confirmation nobody sees is the problem we started with.
          this.setCta('done', this.ctaEl.dataset.added || 'Added', 'tick');
          this.say('Added ' + this.selected + ' to your bag');
          this._doneTimer = window.setTimeout(() => {
            if (this.adding) return;
            this.setCta('ready', this.ctaEl.dataset.add || 'Add to bag', '');
          }, 1100);
        };

        var onAdded = () => settle(true);
        var onError = (e) => settle(false, e && e.detail && e.detail.errorMessage);
        document.addEventListener('ajaxProduct:added', onAdded);
        document.addEventListener('ajaxProduct:error', onError);
        // If the network never answers, the button must not stay stuck.
        this._addTimer = window.setTimeout(() => settle(false, 'That took too long. Please try again.'), 15000);

        btn.click();
      }

      // The bar's height, for the footer runway reserve.
      publishReserve() {
        if (!this.card) return;
        var h = this.card.offsetHeight;
        if (h > 0) document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--onrepeat-sticky-reserve', h + 'px');
      }

      // Whole-rupee INR (mirrors Liquid money-display style 'whole'); US
      // visitors keep theme.money's converted display, like the rest of the
      // theme.
      money(paise) {
        if (paise == null || isNaN(paise)) return '';
        if (window.theme && theme.currencyDisplay && theme.currencyDisplay.usd && theme.money) {
          return theme.money.format(paise);
        }
        return '₹' + Math.round(paise / 100).toLocaleString('en-US');
      }

      moneyNoZeros(paise) {
        if (window.theme && theme.currencyDisplay && theme.currencyDisplay.usd && theme.money) {
          return theme.money.format(paise, 'no_zeros');
        }
        return '₹' + Math.round(paise / 100).toLocaleString('en-US');
      }

      render(variant, chosen) {
        var data = this.variants.filter((v) => v.id === variant.id)[0] || variant;
        var price = data.price;
        if (price == null) return;
        var c = this.cfg;

        if (chosen) this.selected = data.option_value || null;

        // Flat tier first, then the percentage on the remainder — the order
        // Shopify applies automatic discounts in.
        var flat = 0;
        if (c.t3 && price >= c.t3) flat = c.a3;
        else if (c.t2 && price >= c.t2) flat = c.a2;
        // Floor, matching Liquid's integer division in the server render.
        var net = Math.floor(((price - flat) * (100 - c.pct)) / 100);
        var onOffer = c.min > 0 && c.pct > 0 && price >= c.min;

        if (this.netEl) this.netEl.textContent = this.money(onOffer ? net : price);

        var compare = data.compare_at_price;
        var showSale = !onOffer && compare && compare > price;
        if (this.wasEl) this.wasEl.textContent = onOffer ? this.money(price) : (showSale ? this.money(compare) : '');
        if (this.offEl) {
          if (onOffer) {
            this.offEl.textContent = flat > 0
              ? c.pct + '% + ' + this.moneyNoZeros(flat) + ' off applied'
              : c.pct + '% off applied';
          } else if (showSale) {
            this.offEl.textContent = Math.round(((compare - price) / compare) * 100) + '% off';
          } else {
            this.offEl.textContent = '';
          }
        }

        // Stock is only ever stated together with the size it belongs to.
        var qty = data.inventory_quantity;
        var showStock = this.selected && qty != null && qty > 0 && qty <= 3 && data.available !== false;
        // Remembered so an error can borrow the row and hand it back.
        this._stockVisible = !!showStock;
        if (this.stockEl) {
          if (showStock) {
            this.stockEl.textContent = 'Only ' + qty + ' left in ' + this.selected;
            this.stockEl.hidden = false;
          } else {
            this.stockEl.textContent = '';
            this.stockEl.hidden = true;
          }
        }
        if (this.subEl) this.subEl.hidden = !(onOffer || showSale || showStock);

        this.chips.forEach((chip) => {
          chip.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(chip.dataset.size === this.selected));
        });

        // Hand the chosen size to any sheet trigger in the bar. onrepeat-pdp-size-gate
        // does this from the variant picker's checked radio, but that picker is
        // no longer on the page, so the rail is now the only thing that knows.
        Array.prototype.forEach.call(this.querySelectorAll('[data-sleek-open]'), (t) => {
          t.dataset.selected = this.selected || '';
        });

        // An add in flight owns the button until it settles — a variant
        // re-render must not wipe the spinner out from under it.
        if (this.ctaEl && !this.ctaEl.disabled && !this.adding) {
          if (data.available === false) {
            this.setCta('gone', this.ctaEl.dataset.soldOut || 'Sold out', '');
          } else if (this.selected) {
            window.clearTimeout(this._doneTimer);
            this.setCta('ready', this.ctaEl.dataset.add || 'Add to bag', '');
          }
        }
        // A new size is a new attempt; the previous failure no longer applies.
        if (chosen) this.showError('');
      }
    }

    customElements.define('onrepeat-buy-bar', OnRepeatBuyBar);
  })();
</script>
